From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:47:06 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] syscall: set the modification time Utimes is given

Backported from upstream (CL 764480, commit 6f4a698, Go 1.27).

syscall.Utimes checks the access time where it should check the
modification time (CL 219638, commit 5a9b643, Go 1.21), on every Windows,
and Go 1.26 still has that slip. os.Chtimes goes through UtimesNano and was
always right.

Make Utimes set the modification time it is given. Check the modification
time where it checked the access time.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	zero mtime, atime set  mtime moves to 1970    mtime kept
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	mtime set, zero atime  mtime dropped          mtime set

Gate: none | Remembered: N/A

diff --git a/src/syscall/syscall_windows.go b/src/syscall/syscall_windows.go
index ea3bca0a..fb0dd902 100644
--- a/src/syscall/syscall_windows.go
+++ b/src/syscall/syscall_windows.go
@@ -1040,7 +1040,7 @@ func Utimes(path string, tv []Timeval) (err error) {
 	if tv[0].Nanoseconds() != 0 {
 		a = NsecToFiletime(tv[0].Nanoseconds())
 	}
-	if tv[0].Nanoseconds() != 0 {
+	if tv[1].Nanoseconds() != 0 {
 		w = NsecToFiletime(tv[1].Nanoseconds())
 	}
 	return SetFileTime(h, nil, &a, &w)
